; narrator.wyoming -- on-target test runner (Copperline / real A2065 + Roadshow)
;
; AmigaDOS script, auto-run from the system drive's S:User-Startup, which
; picks this over plain `boot` by probing for Copperline's identification
; board (build/amiga/iscopperline -- FindConfigDev(5192, 2), see that
; source file) rather than checking whether a driver file exists: Roadshow's
; DEVS:networks/a2065.device lives on this same shared disk either way, so
; only a real board probe can tell Copperline and Amiberry apart.
;
; Unlike `boot`, networking here goes through a real Zorro A2065 (Am7990
; LANCE) board and a real TCP/IP stack (Roadshow), not a host-sockets
; shortcut -- so CMD_WRITE only works once Roadshow has actually brought the
; interface up. See config/copperline-narrator.toml's [a2065] section for the
; emulator side (net = "nat"/"bridge").

CD Narrator:
Stack 131072

; --- TODO: start Roadshow and wait for the interface to come up ---
; Exact command/config depends on how Roadshow was installed on the shared
; HardDrives/narrator volume (not done yet as of this script -- fill in once
; installed and confirmed on-target). Likely shape:
;
;   Run >NIL: TCP:C/StartNet
;   WaitForPort ... ; or a fixed Wait/link-check loop
;
; Do NOT copy the rest of `boot` below until this actually brings up the
; interface -- otherwise CMD_WRITE will just fail with a connect error
; identical to the failtest.log unreachable-host scenario.

; Install runtime prefs (server address + voice mapping) where the device
; reads them, same as `boot`.
Copy >NIL: Narrator:config/narrator.wyoming ENV:narrator.wyoming
Copy >NIL: Narrator:build/amiga/narrator.device   DEVS:narrator.device
Copy >NIL: Narrator:build/amiga/translator.library LIBS:translator.library

; --- Say acceptance test (the drop-in goal: stock Say -> our device) ---
Echo "narrator.wyoming Say test starting (Copperline / Roadshow / A2065)"
SYS:Utilities/Say "Hello world. This is the Amiga, speaking with a neural voice over Wyoming and A.H.I."
IF WARN
  Echo "*** Say returned WARN/ERROR ***"
  Why
EndIF
Echo "narrator.wyoming Say test done. (window held open 30s for inspection)"
Wait 30
